Maximum fibres in those final boxes are respectively 5,530; 2,048;
2,048; 64; 233; 969; and 32,768. These are measured finite maxima,
except that the MHT empty-edge maximum has the elementary all-size
proof stated in the proof package. No all-size extrapolation is made
from the other measured maxima.

The five family-map boxes are $n=0,\ldots,4$; UPC has seven boxes
$n=0,\ldots,6$; AKC has nine boxes $n=0,\ldots,8$; TDP has the ten
predeclared grids. The original six-rule pilot has 41 boxes and 241,420
state/map pairs. MHT adds five boxes and 65,814 pairs: total **46 boxes,
307,234 state/map pairs**. No random sampling or cutoff increases were
used. Desk-only exclusions are not counted as executed attempts.

## What was actually proved

For UPC, let $P$ be the source reachability poset, $C$ its covers,
$Q$ its noncover chain intervals, and $B$ the remaining comparable
pairs. Order $Q$ by interval inclusion. For $S=A\cap Q$,

$$F(A)=C\cup(Q\setminus\uparrow S).$$

If $M=\min Q$, recurrent states are exactly
$C\cup\{q\in Q:M\cap\downarrow q\subseteq T\}$ for $T\subseteq M$.
The core has $2^{|M|}$ states; height is zero for $n\leq3$ and sharp
two for every $n\geq4$. A target containing a branching interval or
having a non-downset $Q$ part has no source. Otherwise, putting
$D=Q\setminus(Y\cap Q)$, every inverse is obtained by taking all
covers, all of $\min D$, arbitrary remaining members of $D$, and
arbitrary members of $B$. Its fibre is
$2^{|B|+|D|-|\min D|}$. These are full deductions of old closure
mechanics, not residual novelty.

For TDP, every nonempty output is the ambient set intersected with a
convex depth region. Every later output is a nonempty subset of its
predecessor. The resulting generic tail bound is the number of
ambient points, not the height-two pattern seen in these boxes.

For MHT, the minimum edge sizes decrease on each parity subsequence;
once they stabilize, the families grow on those subsequences and
eventually form a one- or two-cycle. The unique largest fibre for
$n\geq1$ consists of all families containing the empty edge, of size
$2^{2^n-1}$. Neither argument supplies a new independent axis.

